                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Collier</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bacon states that the following are names of special embassy and suite:</p>
                <p>Ambassador Frederick Wallingford Whitridge, Mrs. Whitridge, Miss Whitridge;
                    William H. Buckley, secretary; Lieut. Ulysses S. Grant, military attaché; Lieut.
                    Leigh C. Palmer, naval attaché.)</p>
            </div>
